stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Establishing
  Establishing --> CollisionBlocked: active-lane index already owns this scope
  CollisionBlocked --> Closed: one deduped blocker and no writes
  Establishing --> PendingStartup: surface resolved, worktree verified, status artifact created
  PendingStartup --> Acknowledged: exactly one visible acknowledgement delivered
  Acknowledged --> Running: acknowledgement barrier records the provider receipt
  Running --> Running: checkpoint emitted at a named phase
  Running --> ApprovalWait: approval boundary reached
  ApprovalWait --> Running: matching token resumes the same lane
  Running --> LeaseOrphaned: owning process no longer alive
  LeaseOrphaned --> Running: dead-owner proof and diff inventory admit generation N plus 1
  Running --> Terminal: status artifact reaches a terminal state
  Terminal --> FinalReserved: terminal dispatch claim created exclusively
  FinalReserved --> Closed: one visible final carrying a provider message id
  Closed --> [*]
  note right of Running
    The write lease binds root run id, lane generation, status artifact identity
    and runtime owner. Ownership, not state alone, is what makes the lane durable.
  end note
  note right of ApprovalWait
    Parked state stores owner, deadline and resume action, so a restart
    resumes in the same lane rather than opening a second writer.
  end note
